# Local configuration for the web app (Next.js). Copy to .env.local.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ENV=local
# Fixture mode, and `false` is the only honest default. `USE_MOCKS` is read by exactly two
# functions in src/lib/api/client.ts (listMeetings, getMeeting), so `true` gives a quickstart
# where the dashboard and the meeting detail render from src/fixtures/ and every other screen
# fails against a backend that is not there — eight broken screens instead of one clear failure
# at the first request. The client already defaults to `false` for the same reason (a build that
# forgot the variable used to serve fixtures in production); this file now agrees with it.
# Set it to `true` deliberately, to look at those two screens with no backend running.
NEXT_PUBLIC_USE_MOCKS=false
